Concept: Valles Marineris
Description: A vast canyon system on Mars approximately 4000 km long and 7 km deep, located near the equator, roughly 5-20S latitude and 270-330E longitude.
Also known as: valles marineris, mariner valley, vallis marineris, martian grand canyon, the great canyon of mars
Type: Geographic region
Grounds to these fields:
  west -> Bounding_Coordinates.west_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 270, 'unit': 'deg'}
  east -> Bounding_Coordinates.east_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 330, 'unit': 'deg'}
  south -> Bounding_Coordinates.south_bounding_coordinate: {'value': -20, 'unit': 'deg'}
  north -> Bounding_Coordinates.north_bounding_coordinate: {'value': -5, 'unit': 'deg'}

Concept: Tharsis Plateau
Description: A large volcanic highland on Mars, centered near the equator around 250E longitude, featuring the largest volcanoes in the solar system.
Also known as: tharsis, tharsis plateau, tharsis rise, tharsis bulge, tharsis volcanic region
Type: Geographic region
Grounds to these fields:
  west -> Bounding_Coordinates.west_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 220, 'unit': 'deg'}
  east -> Bounding_Coordinates.east_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 280, 'unit': 'deg'}
  south -> Bounding_Coordinates.south_bounding_coordinate: {'value': -20, 'unit': 'deg'}
  north -> Bounding_Coordinates.north_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 30, 'unit': 'deg'}

Concept: Mars Polar Regions
Description: The north and south polar regions of Mars, defined as latitudes above 60N or below 60S. Contains polar ice caps and layered deposits.
Also known as: polar region, north pole, south pole, polar cap, polar ice cap, arctic region mars, polar layered deposits, NPLD, SPLD, north polar layered deposits, south polar layered deposits
Type: Geographic region
Grounds to these fields:
  Region variant 1:
    west -> Bounding_Coordinates.west_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 0, 'unit': 'deg'}
    east -> Bounding_Coordinates.east_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 360, 'unit': 'deg'}
    south -> Bounding_Coordinates.south_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 60, 'unit': 'deg'}
    north -> Bounding_Coordinates.north_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 90, 'unit': 'deg'}
  Region variant 2:
    west -> Bounding_Coordinates.west_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 0, 'unit': 'deg'}
    east -> Bounding_Coordinates.east_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 360, 'unit': 'deg'}
    south -> Bounding_Coordinates.south_bounding_coordinate: {'value': -90, 'unit': 'deg'}
    north -> Bounding_Coordinates.north_bounding_coordinate: {'value': -60, 'unit': 'deg'}

Concept: Hellas Basin
Description: The largest impact basin on Mars, approximately 7 km below datum, located in the southern hemisphere southeast of Tharsis, roughly 30-50S latitude and 50-90E longitude.
Also known as: hellas, hellas basin, hellas planitia, hellas impact basin, hellas crater
Type: Geographic region
Grounds to these fields:
  west -> Bounding_Coordinates.west_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 50, 'unit': 'deg'}
  east -> Bounding_Coordinates.east_bounding_coordinate: {'value': 90, 'unit': 'deg'}
  south -> Bounding_Coordinates.south_bounding_coordinate: {'value': -50, 'unit': 'deg'}
  north -> Bounding_Coordinates.north_bounding_coordinate: {'value': -30, 'unit': 'deg'}

Concept: HiRISE High-Resolution Imaging
Description: High Resolution Imaging Science Experiment on MRO, providing the highest resolution images of Mars surface at sub-meter scale (0.25-0.5 m/pixel).
Also known as: hirise, high resolution imaging, sub-meter imagery, high res camera, color imaging MRO, 25cm resolution
Type: Instrument
Grounds to these fields:
  instrument_name -> Instrument.name: {'value': 'HIRISE'}
  mission_name -> Mission_PDS3.mission_name: {'value': 'MARS RECONNAISSANCE ORBITER'}
  pixel_resolution -> Coordinate_Representation.pixel_resolution_x: {'max': 0.5, 'unit': 'm/pixel'}

Concept: CTX Context Camera
Description: Context Camera on MRO providing wide-field grayscale images at approximately 6 m/pixel resolution over a 30 km swath.
Also known as: ctx, context camera, context imager, 6 meter resolution, wide angle camera MRO, 30km swath, context imagery
Type: Instrument
Grounds to these fields:
  instrument_name -> Instrument.name: {'value': 'CTX'}
  mission_name -> Mission_PDS3.mission_name: {'value': 'MARS RECONNAISSANCE ORBITER'}
  pixel_resolution -> Coordinate_Representation.pixel_resolution_x: {'min': 5.0, 'max': 7.0, 'unit': 'm/pixel'}

Concept: MRO Aerobraking Phase
Description: The aerobraking phase of the Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter mission in 2006, during which limited science data was collected due to non-science orbit geometry.
Also known as: aerobraking, aerobraking phase, MRO aerobraking, 2006 aerobraking, orbital insertion phase, pre-science phase MRO
Type: Mission phase
Grounds to these fields:
  phase_name -> Mission_Phase.mission_phase_name: {'value': 'AEROBRAKING'}
  mission_name -> Mission_PDS3.mission_name: {'value': 'MARS RECONNAISSANCE ORBITER'}
  start -> Time_Coordinates.start_date_time: {'value': '2006-03-01'}
  stop -> Time_Coordinates.stop_date_time: {'value': '2006-08-30'}
